  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Embecta’s core U.S. insulin injection franchise is facing intensifying competitive pressure, customer-specific share losses, and softening market trends, particularly in pen needles. The international business has held steadier, but the U.S. weakness—which represents roughly half of the company’s revenue—drove a sharp quarterly miss and prompted a significant full-year guidance cut. In response to these headwinds, Embecta is pushing a diversification narrative, aiming to broaden its exposure through GLP-1 device opportunities and the pending acquisition of Owen Mumford, a move intended to reduce reliance on the challenged core injection business.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership acknowledged the quarter as a clear disappointment and moved swiftly on multiple fronts. The company initiated a review of its cost structure and organizational footprint, while the board authorized a $100 million share repurchase program alongside a dividend reduction, signaling a shift in capital allocation priorities. Guidance was reset conservatively to reflect U.S. realities and the Owen Mumford deal impact. The CEO is betting that the Owen Mumford acquisition and a push into GLP-1 delivery will transform the portfolio, but near-term execution credibility is being tested.",
